<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10125" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-fingo</span></b> , finxi, fictum, 3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to form,
				fashion, fabricate</i> (class., esp. in a trop. signif.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nidos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					10, 32, 47, § 91</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">favos et ceras,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					11, 5, 4, § 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verbum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 7</span></i>
			 Müll.; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 37, 12, 74, §
			195</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to invent, devise,
				feign, pretend</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dolum inter sese,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt. prol. 35</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 47</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacrimas dolis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					And. 3, 3, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnia haec,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Phorm. 1, 2, 81</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">falsas causas ad discordiam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Hec. 4, 4, 71</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquid criminis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 2, 37, § 90</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crimen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					40, 8, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">40, 42, 4</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Suet. Claud. 15</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquam probabilem causam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					34, 21, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					1, 8, 4</span></i>
			: fronte confictā, * <i><span class="en">Quint. 12,
				3, 12</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homicidium in se,</span>”
				<i>to declare one's self guilty of</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					48, 18, 1</span></i>
			.—With acc. and <i>inf.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">id cogitatum esse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Deiot. 6, 16</span></i>
			.—<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">confingere et comminisci,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 2, 8, 12</span></i>
			. </div>
